body:
@vitaly-zdanevich can you try this appimage? https://github.com/Samueru-sama/Steam-appimage/releases/tag/continuous

I've bundled xdg-desktop-portal-gtk but turns out that it doesn't work, it needs to be installed on the host for some reason.

If I can't find a way to get the portal to work in the appimage then I don't see a point in bundling in it.

I'm not a gamer, and all I know about battle.net is from the option of my Diablo II LOD, from year 2000.

But I think that if there is an Arch Linux package for this, its enough to fork or copy this repo and change all "steam" references for what you're looking for.

@Samueru-sama what do you think about?

@Samueru-sama it seems that we forgot to add lib32-glib

also the AUR package lib32-glibc-eac-bin says that the latter is required by lib32-glib

https://aur.archlinux.org/packages/lib32-glibc-eac-bin?all_reqs=1#pkgreqs

@kenderipa You only have this issue with the appimage right? 

Can you try with [conty](https://github.com/Kron4ek/Conty) as well? 

I've used the appimage with BeamNG (proton) and CS2 (native) and haven't had issues.

@sinetek The next appimage release which will happen after this [PR](https://github.com/ivan-hc/Steam-appimage/pull/28) gets merged will make `.DirIcon` an image and not a symlink, maybe this will fix the issue you have.

I have a feeling that the problem is that DirIcon is a symlink and not an image and as result KDE has trouble picking up, after reading some comments from an unrelated thing lol.

Edit: Now it is merge, try the appimage and let me know.

@Samueru-sama I just tested https://github.com/Samueru-sama/Steam-appimage/releases/tag/continuous

It works well for RimWorld, I think the fix is taking effect.
Haven't been able to test the "extract" though.

@kenderipa I tested with a GTX1060 and it correctly downloads the nvidia drivers and I dont see any performance issues: 

![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/82862019-d3ee-4a62-b379-75594af37414)

I did notice however that it uses the same `$XDG_DATA_HOME/Conty` directory to download the drivers, maybe it is not compatible if it was already downloaded by conty? Try deleting that directory and see.

@Samueru-sama 
> kender@Kender:~$ steam rim-shell -c nvidia-smi

I don't see a problem with the nvidia driver in the container, I also checked this appimage myself and didn't notice any performance degradation.

@VHSgunzo,

